  "result": "I've written the plan, but I haven't changed any code, because plan mode is active. I couldn't call ExitPlanMode, since it isn't among my available tools, so this message is my approval request: tell me to go ahead and I'll implement it.\n\nThe plan file is at `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\add-a-new-parameter-purring-mccarthy.md`.\n\n- **The type:** `KeyValue` goes in `src/click/types.py` next to `UUIDParameterType`, in the same style. `convert` splits on the first `=`. If there's no `=` or the key is empty, it fails with `'<value>' is not a valid key=value pair.`\n- **Value handling:** `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`, and `a=` gives `(\"a\", \"\")`. A tuple that's already converted, such as a default, passes through unchanged.\n- **Export:** one line in `src/click/__init__.py`, in alphabetical position.\n- **Tests:** new cases in `tests/test_types.py` for valid input, both failure modes with the message text, and an end-to-end run through `@click.option(\"--set\", type=click.KeyValue())`. There's also a case in `tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n- **Docs:** an entry in `docs/api.md` and a bullet in `docs/parameter-types.md`.\n- **Changelog:** a bullet in `CHANGES.md`. There is no `CHANGES.rst` in this repo.\n\nI'll check the work by running `pytest` and trying `--set a=b` and `--set abc` in a small script.",
